@startuml CloudWarehouse_Use_Case_Diagram
left to right direction
title System Use Case Diagram

actor "Warehouse Admin" as Admin
actor "Supplier\n(indirect)" as Supplier
actor "System\n(scheduled / background)" as Sys

rectangle "CloudWarehouse System" {

  package "Master Data Management" {
    usecase "Create Site" as UC1
    usecase "Update Site" as UC2
    usecase "Delete Site" as UC3
    usecase "Create Destination" as UC4
    usecase "Update Destination" as UC5
    usecase "Delete Destination" as UC6
  }

  package "Price Table Management" {
    usecase "Download Standard Template" as UC7
    usecase "Upload Price Table Preview" as UC8
    usecase "Confirm Import Price Table" as UC9
    usecase "Export Price Table Result" as UC10
    usecase "Execute Data Validation" as UC11
    usecase "View Import Error Details" as UC12
  }

  package "Core Business" {
    usecase "View Price Rule List" as UC13
    usecase "Calculate Shipping Fee" as UC14
  }
}

Admin --> UC1
Admin --> UC2
Admin --> UC3
Admin --> UC4
Admin --> UC5
Admin --> UC6
Admin --> UC7
Admin --> UC8
Admin --> UC9
Admin --> UC10
Admin --> UC13
Admin --> UC14

Supplier ..> UC8 : provides Excel file
Supplier ..> UC9 : provides Excel file

Sys --> UC11

UC9 ..> UC11 : <<include>>
UC12 ..> UC9 : <<extend>>
note right of UC9
  extension point:
  import failed
end note

@enduml

' 1. Warehouse admin is the primary actor; supplier only supplies files indirectly.
' 2. Use cases follow the business flow: master data, price table import, then rules and fee trial.
' 3. Confirm import includes validation; failed imports extend to error detail review.
